[1.007, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[1.01, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[1.009, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[0.511, "o", "  \u001b[0;90m╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[0.41, "o", "  \u001b[0;90m╭─ \u001b[0m\u001b[1mWhy not use Qwen3-4B as it ships?\u001b[0;90m ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "  \u001b[0;90m│\u001b[0m Off the shelf, Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 reasons in text and does the arithmetic in its head. Fine-tuning on\u001b[0m      \u001b[0;90m│\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "  \u001b[0;90m│\u001b[0m ReTool-SFT traces (SFT) teaches it to run code mid-solution and carry on from the output: this run starts from\u001b[0m \u001b[0;90m│\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "  \u001b[0;90m│\u001b[0m that checkpoint, font-info/qwen3-4b-sft-SGLang-RL. RL then teaches when and how to use the tool, rewarding\u001b[0m     \u001b[0;90m│\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "  \u001b[0;90m│\u001b[0m only the final answer.\u001b[0m                                                                                         \u001b[0;90m│\u001b[0m\r\n"]
